Changes made by FlashRT (2026-11-15)
  - Renamed copy-drift-audit to vla-copy-drift-audit. Rewrote the
    description and added Chinese trigger words.
  - Replaced the ApxInf scope (crates/apxinf-model/src/<backend>_<family>
    copied from <family>, model-family boundary scripts, ops-contract
    surface) with three FlashRT targets:
      (a) a patch/port candidate whose snapshot base_commit is older than the
          current baseline;
      (b) vendored upstream reference code (training/_vendor/openpi_pi0_pytorch,
          csrc/attention/*_src, the FastWAM upstream pin, hy_trace observers);
      (c) third_party/agent-skills and the adapted vla-* skills.
  - Generalized the watermark symbols (P, S, A, B, C, plus T instead of M) to
    FlashRT add commits, recorded upstream pins and snapshot bases. Added stop
    conditions for a missing upstream pin and a non-ancestor base. Added the
    rule to fetch upstream content as data into empty devlocal directories.
  - Kept the method unchanged:
      * one import watermark per file, never --follow, never the last edit;
      * semantic-review-only files;
      * git merge-file -p probes and their exit-code meaning;
      * dispositions absorbed / absorb-now / decline / pending;
      * reverse findings;
      * hunk-by-hunk absorption and no whole-file copy;
      * the clean / drift pending / blocked verdict;
      * "a text audit is not numerical proof".
  - Relaxed the upstream "do not add a script or CI gate" rule only as far as
    third_party/agent-skills/verify_vendor.py goes (integrity at the pin), and
    stated that limit explicitly.
  - Added FlashRT consequences:
      * a rebased patch is a new candidate (new patch_ref, snapshot, operator
        gate, campaign);
      * pin bumps update manifest, VENDOR.md and NOTICE together;
      * the decision log is used with an explicit actor.
  - Replaced the PI0.5-on-MUSA worked example with FlashRT target spellings in
    references/flashrt-targets.md. Changed the report location to
    devlocal/<feat>/reports/. Added agents/openai.yaml.
